`\nand `height`, and an `attributes` table. The position is the lower-left\nobject corner relative to the label's upper-left layout origin.\nInline resource rendering is not part of this MVP; sprites use their explicit\ndimensions or a one-em square fallback.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\nlocal objects = label.get_layout_objects(\"#label\")\nfor _, object in ipairs(objects) do\n    if object.type == \"link\" then\n        print(object.attributes.src, object.text_offset, object.text_length)\n    elseif object.type == \"sprite\" then\n        print(object.attributes.src, object.x, object.y, object.width, object.height)\n    end\nend\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/label-lua#label.get_layout_objects:url)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:label.get_layout_objects","jsName":"getLayoutObjects","line":40,"member":"get_layout_objects","modulePath":["label"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the label to inspect","optional":false,"rawName":"url","rawType":"string|hash|url"}],"rawName":"label.get_layout_objects","returnDescriptions":["objects layout objects in source order"],"returns":["label.layout_object[]"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-bridge","source":"doc/label.lua"},{"description":"Gets the text from a label component\n\nThis function is deprecated. Use `go.get(\"#label\", \"text\")` instead.\n\n**Examples:**\n\n```lua\nfunction init(self)\n    local text = go.get(\"#label\", \"text\")\n    print(text)\nend\n```\n\n[Open in Browser](https://defold.com/ref/label-lua#label.get_text:url)","disposition":"generated-lua-bridge","generics":[],"id":"script:label.get_text","jsName":"getText","line":58,"member":"get_text","modulePath":["label"],"overloads":[],"parameters":[{"description":"the label to get the text from","optional":false,"rawName":"url","rawType":"string|hash|url"}],"rawName":"label.get_text","returnDescriptions":["text the label text"],"returns":["string"],"runtimeStatus":"requires-universal-lua-